u're right to be skeptical of a system that puts the burden on rushed voters. But well-designed e-voting systems don't do that. They use the paper trail as a **verification tool for officials**, not as a human firewall. That's a crucial distinction. So while I understand why the "voter checking a slip for a few seconds" sounds flimsy, the actual security model is far stronger: it's a professional, multi-partisan, statistically rigorous audit that catches errors hackers can't easily hide. That's something we can trust far more than a purely paper-based system with no independent electronic check.
